  "Question": "When using the converse of the Pythagorean theorem to determine whether a triangle is a right triangle, which side should be taken as the hypotenuse when checking \\(a^2+b^2=c^2\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The shortest side",
    "B": "Any side",
    "C": "The longest side"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The hypotenuse is the longest side of a right triangle, so compare the square of the longest side with the sum of the squares of the other two sides.",
